What is the difference between a Compiler-Error and Exception?

A compiler error is caused during the compile time of the program.
This does not allow the JVM to conert to bytecode

Compiler Error is caused when there are mistakes or errors in the Syntax,Method variables,Assignment mismatches,mistakes whle passing the parameters.


An exception is caused when unexpected  events that affect the normal flow of the program.The exceptions cannot be anticipated during the compile time.

Types of exception are
1.Nullpointer exception
2.Arithmeticoperation exception
3.IOexception
4.ArrayIndexOutofBoundsexception
5.ClassNotFoundException
